    "recipe": "Own 16x16 SVG with a lime rectangle at (4,4), size 8x8. Use the recorded root style/attributes and child attributes. Definitions: clipPath half is a rectangle at (0,0), size 8x16; filter f has user-space region (0,0,16,16) and one blue feFlood. rgbaCounts entries are [red,green,blue,alpha,pixelCount]. All sources are own controls, not hosted snippets.",
    "findings": [
      "Background remains canvas paint under root opacity/visibility and root clipping. Border paint follows element opacity/visibility while its content-origin offset survives hidden visibility.",
      "A 3px border moves lime bounds from [4,4,12,12] to [7,7,15,15]; asymmetric widths and padding move the origin by their own edges.",
      "In these fixed-size image controls, box-sizing and an identity viewBox do not alter the layout. This does not qualify other sizing/viewBox contexts.",
      "Fractional fixed border widths resolve to used CSS widths: .25px, 1.5px and 1pt produce one-pixel borders in this image context.",
      "The flood fills the whole viewport; equal flood output cannot establish whether canvas paint participates in filter source capture. The separate accepted child SourceAlpha control protects that boundary."
    ],
    "closure": "Canvas and root generation close. Border/content maps, mixed edge/color alpha, nontrivial viewBox/aspect, fractional sizing/output density, padding and visibility need independent controls before layout admission. Root filters and root clip paths retain explicit scope refusals."
  },
